        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #41308.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3459275441\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41308\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/41308/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41308\">#41308</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The linked issue points out that it isn't just any mouse movement that causes user activation. This makes it clear that it is \"direct and meaningful interaction\", and lists the specific events</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41324",
            "title": "Sticky/transient activation - clarify causes",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-30T13:59:52.000Z",
