        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72118807?u=660cc056ebe508ca2bb205185995d3d2afdbb995&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Remove incorrect <code class=\"notranslate\">font-family: emoji</code> references from the CSS font-family documentation and add a note directing users to the correct <code class=\"notranslate\">font-variant-emoji</code> property.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The documentation incorrectly suggested that <code class=\"notranslate\">font-family: emoji</code> is a standard or supported value, when it's not supported by any browsers. This was misleading developers who might try to use this non-existent syntax. The correct approach for emoji presentation is to use the <code class=\"notranslate\">font-variant-emoji</code> property instead.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Removed <code class=\"notranslate\">font-family: emoji</code> from syntax examples and generic family descriptions</li>\n<li>Removed <code class=\"notranslate\">.emoji</code> CSS class and corresponding HTML example</li>\n<li>Added note with proper GFM syntax directing users to <code class=\"notranslate\">font-variant-emoji</code> property</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">font-variant-emoji</code> has limited browser support (Chrome 131+, Edge 131+, Firefox 141+, but not Safari)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #41093.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3403065943\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41093\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/41093/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41093\">#41093</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41281",
            "title": "Remove font-family: emoji references, add font-variant-emoji note",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-25T18:44:15.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-09-24T18:49:07.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Curis-lab",
                "url": "https://github.com/Curis-lab"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/432915?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">wip</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41267",
            "title": "Document persistent and non-persistent notifications",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-24T15:56:37.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-09-24T04:29:37.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "wbamberg",
                "url": "https://github.com/wbamberg"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/77869922?u=b5f3f9897ce22d8da4dfd442f60757989f73fb38&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Changes</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Add env example (<code class=\"notranslate\">.env-dist</code>) for project environment variables</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Linked Issues: <a href=\"https://github.com/mdn/fred/issues/761\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/fred/issues/761/hovercard\">#761</a></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">^ The following is an issue created in <a href=\"https://github.com/mdn/fred\">FRED repo</a></p>\n</blockquote>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41266",
            "title": "Add env example",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-29T01:51:51.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-09-24T04:28:08.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "brysonbw",
                "url": "https://github.com/brysonbw"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/349114?u=1185d4fc45f5ff4c4a592b30a4dd2bb5cd1b7128&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds a new page to our list of \"attacks\", this one is on JavaScript Prototype Pollution.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Generally, I'm not sure if I covered everything that needs to appear here. I think I'm somewhat happy about the defenses part, but explaining how to actually get into to polluting objects might need some more words?</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Also, I think this needs integration into JS docs (at a minimum some linkage).</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Developing a series of guides about common attacks on websites, explaining for each attack: how it works, the impact, and how to defend against it.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Would love some feedback from <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/wbamberg/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/wbamberg\">@wbamberg</a>, <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/aaronshim/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/aaronshim\">@aaronshim</a> and maybe <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/Josh-Cena/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/Josh-Cena\">@Josh-Cena</a>.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">None, I think.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41260",
            "title": "Add a page for JavaScript prototype pollution attack",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-29T12:25:07.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-09-23T17:43:52.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Elchi3",
                "url": "https://github.com/Elchi3"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 136 introduces the CSS <a href=\"https://drafts.csswg.org/css-color-hdr/#the-dynamic-range-limit-property\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">dynamic-range-limit</code></a> property; see <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5146250411769856\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5146250411769856</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The <code class=\"notranslate\">dynamic-range-limit-mix()</code> function is also supported, but I'm not sure which version of Chrome this first appeared in. I've asked Chrome engineering for an answer to this question.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR documents both of the two features mentioned above.</p>\n<div class=\"markdown-alert markdown-alert-note\" dir=\"auto\"><p class=\"markdown-alert-title\" dir=\"auto\"><svg class=\"octicon octicon-info mr-2\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M0 8a8 8 0 1 1 16 0A8 8 0 0 1 0 8Zm8-6.5a6.5 6.5 0 1 0 0 13 6.5 6.5 0 0 0 0-13ZM6.5 7.75A.75.75 0 0 1 7.25 7h1a.75.75 0 0 1 .75.75v2.75h.25a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.5h-2a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.5h.25v-2h-.25a.75.75 0 0 1-.75-.75ZM8 6a1 1 0 1 1 0-2 1 1 0 0 1 0 2Z\"></path></svg>Note</p><p dir=\"auto\">Some of the description in the property page might want to go into a separate glossary entry, but I wasn't sure how best to chop up this information. Opinions welcome.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41257",
            "title": "Editorial review: Document CSS dynamic-range-limit",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-24T12:32:23.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-09-23T13:42:26.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF144 (and Safari) implement <code class=\"notranslate\">CSSStyleProperties</code>. This is a derived class of <code class=\"notranslate\">CSSStyleDeclaration</code> that represents the inline or computed styles on an element. It exists because  <code class=\"notranslate\">CSSStyleDeclaration</code> is now going to be a base class from which specific types of style and rule information will be applied, and only include the relevant information for that context.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Anyway, this adds the new class and fixes up all the places that return it. It also updates  <code class=\"notranslate\">CSSStyleDeclaration</code>  to note that this is now a base class but didn't used to be.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">There is quite a lot of duplication. Mostly because there was before I started too. I wasn't sure how much to include in say <code class=\"notranslate\">HTMLElement.style</code> and how much to have in the <code class=\"notranslate\">CSSStyleProperties</code> as common. Generally I have kept about the same level in each doc as originally.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3417388824\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41133\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/41133/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41133\">#41133</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41254",
            "title": "FF144 CSSStyleProperties docs",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-30T06:29:00.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-09-23T07:46:30.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF144 adds support for the JS Upsert Proposal in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1979917\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1979917</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This adds a release note that covers the new methods added to <code class=\"notranslate\">Map</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">WeakMap</code>.,</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3417399601\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41134\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/41134/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41134\">#41134</a></p>",
